t"},{"code":"169.254.169.254","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unreachable.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"allowHttp"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy":{"title":"CimdPolicy","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether, and on what terms, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it names (T21.5, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document"},{"type":"text","text":"). # Why this is one nested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — and none of them means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything without ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot ["},{"code":"Self::enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::allow_http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domains or "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument ["},{"code":"OidcPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes for "},{"code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". # Every bound here is a security control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"code":"Self::min_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"code":"Self::max_cache_secs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written by hand cannot lift them."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","title":"AxiamSDK","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"}}}